  "worked_solution": "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n(n+1)!=(n+1)n!\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $n!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n!)^{2}}{((n+1)!)^{2}} & =\\frac{n!\\cdot n!}{(n+1)!\\cdot (n+1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{n!}\\cdot \\cancel{n!}}{(n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{n!}\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{n!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(n+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
